  "title": "Protestant Reformation",
  "summary": "By the traditional account, Martin Luther posted 95 Theses in Latin on the Castle Church door in Wittenberg on 31 October 1517, proposing a debate on indulgences. A copy sent to Archbishop Albrecht went on to Pope Leo X, and a German translation followed in early 1518. The Church response radicalized Luther, and the dispute grew into the Protestant Reformation.",
